                            <comment id="17016658" author="zstan" created="Thu, 16 Jan 2020 08:09:04 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;i run some benchmarks after applying this patch, 3 servers 1 client , persist enabled, partitioned cache, wal log_only, looks good to me.&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/12991086/12991086_screenshot-1.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17017412" author="ivan.glukos" created="Thu, 16 Jan 2020 18:54:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt; Looks good, please merge.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17017925" author="alex_pl" created="Fri, 17 Jan 2020 11:24:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve found one problem, the offheap manager created per cache group, so the limit will affect only one cache group, but not the entire data region. I think the database shared manager is a better place to store limits. I will fix it shortly.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17018062" author="alex_pl" created="Fri, 17 Jan 2020 14:07:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve moved pages list cache limit to the database shared manager and added second cache group to test. &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ivan.glukos&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ivan.glukos&quot;&gt;ivan.glukos&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zstan&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zstan&quot;&gt;zstan&lt;/a&gt;&#160;please have a look again.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
